{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/2","id":4892552996,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVMZGKc8AAAABI55vJA","html_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pull/2.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/issues/2","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/2/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/2/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/issues/2/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/verifiable-execution-claim-authorization/statuses/653b8e92e56afb99797c04b1c616a6d7fb3555e9","number":2,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"research: real-artifact composition v2 with explicit execution limits","user":{"login":"pipavlo82","id":212635108,"node_id":"U_kgDODKyN5A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/212635108?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82","html_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pipavlo82/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem and result\n\nIndividually accepted proofs and signatures can concern different inputs, subjects, actions, executions, policies or domains. This research compares component-only authorization with explicit cross-artifact obligations using retained native zkIE artifacts and genuine laboratory EIP-712 signatures.\n\nThe positive claim is limited to a pinned public MatMul recomputation under a laboratory policy. A complete external WYRIWE -> zkIE -> judgment -> execution chain remains NOT IMPLEMENTED. Offline domains, laboratory authority and signed local observations do not establish external admission or historical execution. No upstream vulnerability, cryptographic soundness theorem, scientific priority or certification is claimed.\n\n## Original v2 evidence\n\n- Main `18a5916098addf6447700ed95441125bfa7079c3` contains v1 `ea89871064e98a67b6ba01c836d498bee89aa437`; main is unchanged.\n- Two retained 380-byte native proofs, separate-process verification and full arithmetic recomputation; ten actual laboratory signature artifacts and Keccak commitments.\n- 26 scenarios, 20 tests in normal/repeat/Python -O. Component-only control falsely authorizes 18/25 negatives; composition authorizes 0/25 with four UNVERIFIABLE outcomes.\n- The frozen original run at `ba889271bef7cb3d2eed00067a12064689bfb627` remains 18 KILLED / 2 SURVIVED / 0 CRASHED. One unavailable historical-execution integration is UNVERIFIABLE and unexecuted.\n\n## Survivor audit\n\nBoth original survivors are non-equivalent mutations with masked original witnesses. For native enforcement, input and provenance bindings independently rejected the original wrong-input case. For artifact type enforcement, signer authority independently rejected the receipt-as-judgment case.\n\nThe follow-up adds isolated witnesses with six genuinely generated laboratory signatures. An explicitly corrupted proof fails only inference; a genuine LabReceipt signed by the judgment-role key fails only artifact type. Removing each exact original source check changes REFUTED to VERIFIED; restoring it restores REFUTED. Positive controls remain VERIFIED. Mutant source hashes match the original run. No verifier logic changes.\n\n- Follow-up: 2 KILLED, 0 SURVIVED, 0 CRASHED, 0 NOT_APPLIED, 0 UNVERIFIABLE.\n- 7 additional tests pass normal/repeat/-O; both targeted tests fail by assertion under their mutants and pass after restoration. Audit snapshots are identical across modes and match on Linux CI.\n- Fresh public checkout `653b8e92e56afb99797c04b1c616a6d7fb3555e9` passes native build and two native tests, original 20 tests in three modes, all new controls and all 755 inventory checks.\n- All three GitHub workflows passed for both push and PR at this SHA. All 496 protected source/fixture/evidence/test/native files remain byte-identical to the original v2 commit.\n\nSee [survivor audit](https://github.com/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/blob/653b8e92e56afb99797c04b1c616a6d7fb3555e9/research/V2_SURVIVOR_AUDIT.md), [original v2 report](https://github.com/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/blob/653b8e92e56afb99797c04b1c616a6d7fb3555e9/research/V2_REAL_ARTIFACT_REPORT.md) and [Linux CI](https://github.com/pipavlo82/verifiable-ai-guarantee-composition/actions/runs/38969191251). Fresh execution and CI are reproducibility evidence, not independent human review. Keep this PR draft; no merge is requested or authorized.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T18:20:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","closed_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","merged_at":"2026-10-21T21:16:13Z","merge_commit_sha":"653b8e92e56afb99797c04b1c616a6d7fb3555e9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"request